BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Holiday Lights Spectacular at Roger Williams Park Zoo
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260104
DTSTAMP:20261124T205212Z
UID:9d954c5bfbb94ce967fa8807d18a@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Bring family and friends to experience Holiday Lights Spectacu
 lar &#8211\; an annual walk-through experience just in time for the holida
 ys. Featuring festive\, larger-than-life dazzling displays\, this year’s
  event boasts more than 3.5 million twinkling lights that transform the Zo
 o into a winter wonderland! Join us and ring in the season nightly from No
 vember 27 through January 3. Bundle up\, grab an adult beverage\, hot choc
 olate\, or roast some s’mores and stroll through 40 acres of illuminated
  pathways. December 4 is Santa's Parade!! Santa visits Friday through Sund
 ay evenings\, December 4 to 20. For full details on specific events and Ti
 ckets please visit the website - tickets must be reserved online in advanc
 e Holiday Lights will be closed on Christmas Eve and Christmas Day. WEATHE
 R POLICY — The Holiday Lights Spectacular is open rain or shine. In the 
 case of light to moderate rain or snow\, the show will be open\; there are
  no refunds. Please check the website or visit Facebook for updates.\n\nSo
 urce: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/holiday-lights-spectacular-at
 -roger-williams-park-zoo/112750/
LOCATION:Roger Williams Park Zoo & Carousel Village\, 1000 Elmwood Avenue
 \, Providence\, RI 02907
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/holiday-lights-spectacular-at-r
 oger-williams-park-zoo/112750/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beyond the Brewhouse Tour
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260515
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260516
DTSTAMP:20261124T205212Z
UID:acc9d8e1d1bdab34c6766b602473@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Beyond the Brewhouse Where: Newport Craft Brewing and Distilli
 ng\, 293 JT Connell Road\, Newport 45 minutes: $20 per person Did you know
  that we are a Distillery too? Going beyond the brewhouse\, our expert tou
 r guide will provide you with an in-depth explanation of our brewing and d
 istilling processes. Tour the brewhouse\, take a peek at our Sour room\, a
 nd walk through our distillery. Conclude the tour with a brew and spirit f
 light for a complete palate experience. Ages 21+\n\nSource: https://www.vi
 sitrhodeisland.com/event/beyond-the-brewhouse-tour/110153/
LOCATION:Newport Craft Brewing & Distilling Company\, 293 JT Connell Road
 \, Newport\, RI 02840 Time: 45 minutes: Tour start time varies by booking.
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/beyond-the-brewhouse-tour/11015
 3/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blithewold Homeschool Days
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260629
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260630
DTSTAMP:20261124T205212Z
UID:2d7c1782c92278d18720700e79bc@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Homeschool Days at Blithewold Last Tuesday of each month Octob
 er 27\, 2026 &#8211\; June 29\, 2027 10:00 AM &#8211\; 12:00 PM Location: 
 Education Room in Visitor’s Center and Grounds Join us on the last Tuesd
 ay of each month\, from October through June\, for fun (and educational) h
 ands-on learning at Blithewold! Each month\, we explore intriguing topics 
 in the arts\, history\, horticulture\, environmental science\, and climate
  change. Indoor and outdoor learning experiences complete our curriculum\,
  which aligns with RI\, MA\, and CT state standards. Check our website for
  more information on our monthly themes and activities. This drop-off prog
 ram is designed for ages 8 &#8211\; 13. Students check in at the Welcome C
 enter. Please bring a refillable water bottle and dress for the weather\, 
 as we often take our lessons outside! Monthly Program Topics: October 27: 
 Blithewold’s Champion Trees &#8211\; What makes them Champions? November
  24: Rising Seas and Climate Change &#8211\; Learn about our new berm and 
 how climate change affects plant\, insect\, and bird breeding cycles. Marc
 h 30: What Are Textiles? History and Methods of Creation &#8211\; Make a t
 extile project to enjoy! April 27: Archives Tour with the Curator &#8211\;
  Learn about the collection items stored behind the scenes and how they’
 re handled and cataloged with our new curator\, Kristen Costa. May 25: Nat
 ure Journaling &#8211\; Learn to capture your time in nature by drawing an
 d writing in a book or journal for future enjoyment. June 29: Pollinators 
 and Native Plants &#8211\; Find out why pollinators are so important to th
 e world and how to provide the food and habitat they need to survive. Cost
 : Nonmember Student $15 | Additional Nonmember Student $12 Member Student 
 $5 | Additional Member Student $4 The programs are designed for ages 8 &#8
 211\; 13 Class size is limited to 15. Reservations are required. Register 
 Here\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/blithewold-homescho
 ol-days/109483/
LOCATION:Education Room in Visitor’s Center and Grounds Join us on the l
 ast Tuesday of each month\, from October through June\, for fun (and educa
 tional) hands-on learning at Blithewold! Each month\, we explore intriguin
 g topics in the arts\, history\, horticulture\, environmental science\, an
 d climate change. Indoor and outdoor learning experiences complete our cur
 riculum\, which aligns with RI\, MA\, and CT state standards. Check our we
 bsite for more information on our monthly themes and activities. This drop
 -off program is designed for ages 8 – 13. Students check in at the Welco
 me Center. Please bring a refillable water bottle and dress for the weathe
 r\, as we often take our lessons outside! Monthly Program Topics: October 
 27: Blithewold’s Champion Trees – What makes them Champions? November 
 24: Rising Seas and Climate Change – Learn about our new berm and how cl
 imate change affects plant\, insect\, and bird breeding cycles. March 30: 
 What Are Textiles? History and Methods of Creation – Make a textile proj
 ect to enjoy! April 27: Archives Tour with the Curator – Learn about the
  collection items stored behind the scenes and how they’re handled and c
 ataloged with our new curator\, Kristen Costa. May 25: Nature Journaling 
 – Learn to capture your time in nature by drawing and writing in a book 
 or journal for future enjoyment. June 29: Pollinators and Native Plants 
 – Find out why pollinators are so important to the world and how to prov
 ide the food and habitat they need to survive. Cost: Nonmember Student $15
  | Additional Nonmember Student $12 Member Student $5 | Additional Member 
 Student $4 The programs are designed for ages 8 – 13 Class size is limit
 ed to 15. Reservations are required. Register Here Show More View Website 
 | Email 1 / 1 Additional Information\, 101 Ferry Road\, Bristol\, RI 02809
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/blithewold-homeschool-days/1094
 83/
END:VEVENT
